====================================================================================
Pre-registered interpretation matrix (based on the non-saturated subset n=80)
====================================================================================
A- — MTL occlusion significantly lowers the true-class probability, significantly more than the volume-matched/random-sphere controls,
      but **MTL has no significant advantage over the hippocampus alone** (p=0.19)
      → supports "the medial temporal lobe carries diagnostic information", but the evidence points to **the hippocampus itself** rather than the whole MTL
      → if the paper claims MTL (rather than hippocampal) specificity, caution is needed

  controls passing correction = 2 / 3
  MTL vs hippocampus p = 0.1904 (no significant difference)

